IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nsw-interpretation-time`

-- Interpretation Act 1987 (New South Wales), Part 11 Miscellaneous: sections 64 to 83. Section 81 is printed "(Repealed)".
-- The time of expiry (section 71), the seventh working day (section 76(1)(b)) and the working day (section 76(2)) are computed in nsw-interpretation-time.l4.

§ `Part 11 Miscellaneous`

§§ `64 Every section of an Act a substantive enactment`

-- src:662 | Every section of an Act has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words.
@ref s 64 (src:662)
GIVEN `it is a section of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64 the section has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words` MEANS
    IF `it is a section of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `64A Schedules`

-- src:665 | A schedule to an Act or instrument has effect according to its tenor when it comes into force, whether or not the Act or instrument declares that the schedule has effect.
@ref s 64A (src:665)
GIVEN `it is a schedule to an Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act or instrument has come into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64A the schedule has effect according to its tenor` MEANS
    IF `it is a schedule to an Act or instrument` THEN JUST `the Act or instrument has come into force` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `65 References to Acts generally`

-- src:668 | An Act passed by Parliament, or by any earlier legislature of New South Wales, may be referred to by the word "Act" alone.
@ref s 65 (src:668)
GIVEN `it is an Act passed by Parliament, or by any earlier legislature of New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65 the Act may be referred to by the word Act alone` MEANS
    IF `it is an Act passed by Parliament, or by any earlier legislature of New South Wales` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `66 Citation of particular Acts`

DECLARE KindOfActCited IS ONE OF
    AnActOfNewSouthWales
    ACommonwealthActCited
    AnActOrOrdinanceOfAnotherStateOrTerritoryCited
    ABritishActCited

DECLARE WayOfCitingAnAct IS ONE OF
    ByItsShortTitleOrName
    ByTheYearInWhichItWasPassedAndItsNumber
    ByTheRegnalYearInWhichItWasPassedAndItsNumber
    InSuchOtherMannerAsIsSufficientInAnActOfThatLegislature
    InAnotherWayOfCitingAnAct

-- src:676 | (2) A Commonwealth Act may be cited—
-- src:677 | (a) by its short title (or name), or
-- src:678 | (b) in such other manner as is sufficient in a Commonwealth Act,
-- src:679 | together with a reference to the Commonwealth.
-- src:680 | (3) An Act or Ordinance of some other State or Territory may be cited—
-- src:681 | (a) by its short title (or name), or
-- src:682 | (b) in such other manner as is sufficient in an Act or Ordinance of that other State or Territory,
-- src:683 | together with a reference to that other State or Territory.
-- src:684 | (4) A British Act may be cited—
-- src:685 | (a) by its short title (or name), or
-- src:686 | (b) in such other manner as is sufficient in a British Act,
-- src:687 | together with a reference to the United Kingdom.
@ref s 66(2) to (4) (src:676-687)
GIVEN way IS A WayOfCitingAnAct
      `the citation is together with a reference to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the kind of Act requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(2) to (4) an Act of another legislature may be cited in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN ByItsShortTitleOrName THEN JUST `the citation is together with a reference to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the kind of Act requires`
    WHEN InSuchOtherMannerAsIsSufficientInAnActOfThatLegislature THEN JUST `the citation is together with a reference to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the kind of Act requires`
    WHEN ByTheYearInWhichItWasPassedAndItsNumber THEN NOTHING
    WHEN ByTheRegnalYearInWhichItWasPassedAndItsNumber THEN NOTHING
    WHEN InAnotherWayOfCitingAnAct THEN NOTHING

-- src:671 | (1) An Act may be cited—
-- src:672 | (a) by its short title (or name), or
-- src:673 | (b) by reference to—
-- src:674 | (i) the year in which it was passed or, in the case of an Act passed before 1897, by reference to the regnal year in which it was passed, and
-- src:675 | (ii) its number.
@ref s 66(1) (src:671-675)
GIVEN kind IS A KindOfActCited
      way IS A WayOfCitingAnAct
      `the Act was passed before 1897` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the citation is together with a reference to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the kind of Act requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66 the Act may be cited in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN AnActOfNewSouthWales THEN
        CONSIDER way
        WHEN ByItsShortTitleOrName THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN ByTheYearInWhichItWasPassedAndItsNumber THEN JUST (NOT `the Act was passed before 1897`)
        WHEN ByTheRegnalYearInWhichItWasPassedAndItsNumber THEN JUST `the Act was passed before 1897`
        WHEN InSuchOtherMannerAsIsSufficientInAnActOfThatLegislature THEN NOTHING
        WHEN InAnotherWayOfCitingAnAct THEN NOTHING
    WHEN ACommonwealthActCited THEN `s 66(2) to (4) an Act of another legislature may be cited in that way` way `the citation is together with a reference to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the kind of Act requires`
    WHEN AnActOrOrdinanceOfAnotherStateOrTerritoryCited THEN `s 66(2) to (4) an Act of another legislature may be cited in that way` way `the citation is together with a reference to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the kind of Act requires`
    WHEN ABritishActCited THEN `s 66(2) to (4) an Act of another legislature may be cited in that way` way `the citation is together with a reference to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the kind of Act requires`

§§ `67 Citation of instruments etc`

DECLARE KindOfInstrumentCited IS ONE OF
    AnInstrumentMadeUnderAnActOfNewSouthWales
    AnInstrumentMadeUnderACommonwealthAct
    AnInstrumentMadeUnderAnActOrOrdinanceOfAnotherStateOrTerritory
    AnInstrumentMadeUnderABritishAct

DECLARE WayOfReferringToAnInstrument IS ONE OF
    ByItsCitationOrName
    ByTheNumberDateAndPagesOfTheGazetteInWhichItWasPublished
    ByTheDateOfItsPublicationOnTheNSWLegislationWebsite
    ByTheDateOnWhichItWasMade
    InSuchOtherMannerAsIsSufficientInAnActOfThatLegislatureForInstruments
    InAnotherWayOfReferringToAnInstrument

-- src:697 | (2) An instrument made under a Commonwealth Act may be referred to—
-- src:698 | (a) by its citation (or name), or
-- src:699 | (b) in such other manner as is sufficient in a Commonwealth Act,
-- src:700 | together with a reference to the Commonwealth.
-- src:701 | (3) An instrument made under an Act or Ordinance of some other State or Territory may be referred to—
-- src:702 | (a) by its citation (or name), or
-- src:703 | (b) in such other manner as is sufficient in an Act or Ordinance of that other State or Territory,
-- src:704 | together with a reference to that other State or Territory.
-- src:705 | (4) An instrument made under a British Act may be referred to—
-- src:706 | (a) by its citation (or name), or
-- src:707 | (b) in such other manner as is sufficient in a British Act,
-- src:708 | together with a reference to the United Kingdom.
@ref s 67(2) to (4) (src:697-708)
GIVEN way IS A WayOfReferringToAnInstrument
      `the reference is together with a reference to the Act under which the instrument was made, or to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the case requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(2) to (4) an instrument made under an Act of another legislature may be referred to in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN ByItsCitationOrName THEN JUST `the reference is together with a reference to the Act under which the instrument was made, or to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the case requires`
    WHEN InSuchOtherMannerAsIsSufficientInAnActOfThatLegislatureForInstruments THEN JUST `the reference is together with a reference to the Act under which the instrument was made, or to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the case requires`
    WHEN ByTheNumberDateAndPagesOfTheGazetteInWhichItWasPublished THEN NOTHING
    WHEN ByTheDateOfItsPublicationOnTheNSWLegislationWebsite THEN NOTHING
    WHEN ByTheDateOnWhichItWasMade THEN NOTHING
    WHEN InAnotherWayOfReferringToAnInstrument THEN NOTHING

-- src:690 | (1) An instrument may be referred to—
-- src:691 | (a) by its citation (or name), or
-- src:692 | (b) by reference to—
-- src:693 | (i) in the case of an instrument that has been published in a printed copy of the Gazette—the number, date and page or pages of the Gazette in which it was published, or
-- src:694 | (ia) in the case of an instrument that has been published on the NSW legislation website—the date of its publication on that website, or
-- src:695 | (ii) in any other case—the date on which it was made,
-- src:696 | together with a reference to the Act under which it was made.
@ref s 67(1) (src:690-696)
GIVEN kind IS A KindOfInstrumentCited
      way IS A WayOfReferringToAnInstrument
      `the instrument has been published in a printed copy of the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument has been published on the NSW legislation website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is together with a reference to the Act under which the instrument was made, or to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the case requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67 the instrument may be referred to in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN AnInstrumentMadeUnderAnActOfNewSouthWales THEN
        CONSIDER way
        WHEN ByItsCitationOrName THEN JUST `the reference is together with a reference to the Act under which the instrument was made, or to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the case requires`
        WHEN ByTheNumberDateAndPagesOfTheGazetteInWhichItWasPublished THEN IF `the instrument has been published in a printed copy of the Gazette` THEN JUST `the reference is together with a reference to the Act under which the instrument was made, or to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the case requires` ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN ByTheDateOfItsPublicationOnTheNSWLegislationWebsite THEN IF `the instrument has been published on the NSW legislation website` THEN JUST `the reference is together with a reference to the Act under which the instrument was made, or to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the case requires` ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN ByTheDateOnWhichItWasMade THEN IF (NOT `the instrument has been published in a printed copy of the Gazette`) AND (NOT `the instrument has been published on the NSW legislation website`) THEN JUST `the reference is together with a reference to the Act under which the instrument was made, or to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the case requires` ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN InSuchOtherMannerAsIsSufficientInAnActOfThatLegislatureForInstruments THEN NOTHING
        WHEN InAnotherWayOfReferringToAnInstrument THEN NOTHING
    WHEN AnInstrumentMadeUnderACommonwealthAct THEN `s 67(2) to (4) an instrument made under an Act of another legislature may be referred to in that way` way `the reference is together with a reference to the Act under which the instrument was made, or to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the case requires`
    WHEN AnInstrumentMadeUnderAnActOrOrdinanceOfAnotherStateOrTerritory THEN `s 67(2) to (4) an instrument made under an Act of another legislature may be referred to in that way` way `the reference is together with a reference to the Act under which the instrument was made, or to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the case requires`
    WHEN AnInstrumentMadeUnderABritishAct THEN `s 67(2) to (4) an instrument made under an Act of another legislature may be referred to in that way` way `the reference is together with a reference to the Act under which the instrument was made, or to the Commonwealth, the other State or Territory, or the United Kingdom, as the case requires`

§§ `68 References to amended or repealed Acts and instruments`

-- src:711 | (1) In any Act or instrument, a reference to some other Act or instrument extends to the other Act or instrument, as in force for the time being.
@ref s 68(1) (src:711)
GIVEN `it is a reference in an Act or instrument to some other Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(1) the reference extends to the other Act or instrument, as in force for the time being` MEANS
    IF `it is a reference in an Act or instrument to some other Act or instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:712 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to a reference to an Act or instrument—
-- src:713 | (a) whether or not the reference includes a reference to subsequent amendments of the Act or instrument, and
-- src:714 | (b) whether or not the reference is to a mode of citation that includes 2 calendar years.
@ref s 68(2) (src:712-714)
GIVEN `it is a reference to an Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference includes a reference to subsequent amendments of the Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mode of citation includes 2 calendar years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(2) section 68(1) applies to the reference` MEANS
    IF `it is a reference to an Act or instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- What a reference to a repealed Act or instrument extends to, section 68(3).
DECLARE ReferenceToARepealedAndReplacedThing IS ONE OF
    AReferenceToAnActRepealedAndReEnacted
    AReferenceToAnInstrumentRepealedAndReMade
    AReferenceToAProvisionOfTheRepealedActOrInstrument
    AReferenceToSomeOtherRepealedThing

-- src:715 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection (1), in any Act or instrument—
-- src:716 | (a) a reference to an Act that has been repealed and re-enacted, with or without modification, extends to the re-enacted Act, as in force for the time being, and
-- src:717 | (b) a reference to an instrument that has been repealed and re-made, with or without modification, extends to the re-made instrument, as in force for the time being,
-- src:718 | and a reference to a provision of the repealed Act or instrument extends to the corresponding provision of the re-enacted Act or the re-made instrument, as the case may be.
@ref s 68(3) (src:715-718)
GIVEN reference IS A ReferenceToARepealedAndReplacedThing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(3) the reference extends to the re-enacted Act, the re-made instrument or the corresponding provision, as in force for the time being` MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN AReferenceToAnActRepealedAndReEnacted THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AReferenceToAnInstrumentRepealedAndReMade THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AReferenceToAProvisionOfTheRepealedActOrInstrument THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AReferenceToSomeOtherRepealedThing THEN NOTHING

-- src:719 | (3A) Nothing in this section affects the operation of sections 11 and 12 of the Corporations (Ancillary Provisions) Act 2001.
@ref s 68(3A) (src:719)
GIVEN `it is the operation of sections 11 and 12 of the Corporations (Ancillary Provisions) Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68 affects the operation of the other provisions` MEANS
    IF `it is the operation of sections 11 and 12 of the Corporations (Ancillary Provisions) Act 2001` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- What a reference to an Act includes in section 68, subsection (4)(a). "includes" leaves the list open.
DECLARE WhatAReferenceToAnActIncludes IS ONE OF
    ACommonwealthActIncluded
    AnActOrOrdinanceOfAnotherStateOrTerritoryIncluded
    ABritishActIncluded
    OneOfTheFiveCodesNamedInParagraphIv
    TheASICLawOfNewSouthWales
    TheCorporationsLawOfNewSouthWales
    TheAFICAndFinancialInstitutionsCodes
    TheNationalElectricityNSWLaw
    TheFriendlySocietiesNSWCode
    TheNationalGasNSWLaw
    SomethingElseNotNamed

-- src:720 | (4) In this section—
-- src:721 | (a) a reference to an Act includes a reference to—
-- src:722 | (i) a Commonwealth Act, and
-- src:723 | (ii) an Act or Ordinance of some other State or Territory, and
-- src:724 | (iii) a British Act, and
-- src:725 | (iv) the Companies (New South Wales) Code, the Companies (Acquisition of Shares) (New South Wales) Code, the Securities Industry (New South Wales) Code, the Futures Industry (New South Wales) Code and the Companies and Securities (Interpretation and Miscellaneous Provisions) (New South Wales) Code, and
-- src:726 | (v) the ASIC Law of New South Wales, and
-- src:727 | (vi) the Corporations Law of New South Wales, and
-- src:728 | (vii) the AFIC (NSW) Code and the Financial Institutions (NSW) Code, and
-- src:729 | (viia) the National Electricity (NSW) Law, and
-- src:730 | (viii) the Friendly Societies (NSW) Code, and
-- src:731 | (ix) the National Gas (NSW) Law,
-- src:732 | (b) a reference to an instrument includes a reference to an instrument made under such an Act or Ordinance.
@ref s 68(4) (src:720-732)
GIVEN included IS A WhatAReferenceToAnActIncludes
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(4)(a) a reference to an Act includes a reference to the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER included
    WHEN ACommonwealthActIncluded THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AnActOrOrdinanceOfAnotherStateOrTerritoryIncluded THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN ABritishActIncluded THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN OneOfTheFiveCodesNamedInParagraphIv THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN TheASICLawOfNewSouthWales THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN TheCorporationsLawOfNewSouthWales THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN TheAFICAndFinancialInstitutionsCodes THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN TheNationalElectricityNSWLaw THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN TheFriendlySocietiesNSWCode THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN TheNationalGasNSWLaw THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN SomethingElseNotNamed THEN NOTHING

-- src:732 | (b) a reference to an instrument includes a reference to an instrument made under such an Act or Ordinance.
@ref s 68(4)(b) (src:732)
GIVEN `it is an instrument made under an Act or Ordinance that section 68(4)(a) includes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(4)(b) a reference to an instrument includes a reference to the instrument` MEANS
    IF `it is an instrument made under an Act or Ordinance that section 68(4)(a) includes` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:733 | (5) This section extends to a reference to a repealed Act or instrument that is replaced by Commonwealth legislation (including legislation enacted in reliance on a referral of legislative power by the State).
@ref s 68(5) (src:733)
GIVEN `it is a reference to a repealed Act or instrument that is replaced by Commonwealth legislation, including legislation enacted in reliance on a referral of legislative power by the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(5) section 68 extends to the reference` MEANS
    IF `it is a reference to a repealed Act or instrument that is replaced by Commonwealth legislation, including legislation enacted in reliance on a referral of legislative power by the State` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `69 References to publications other than Acts or instruments`

-- The day as at which a publication is read, or no fixed day.
DECLARE PointAtWhichAPublicationIsRead IS ONE OF
    AsInForceOrCurrentOnTheDay HAS readingDay IS A DATE
    AsInForceForTheTimeBeing

-- src:736 | (1) In any Act or instrument, a reference to a publication other than an Act or instrument is a reference to the publication—
-- src:737 | (a) if a particular day is specified for that purpose in the Act or instrument—as in force or current on that particular day, or
-- src:738 | (b) in any other case—as in force or current on the day on which the provision containing the reference took effect.
@ref s 69(1) (src:736-738)
GIVEN `a particular day is specified for that purpose in the Act or instrument` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the provision containing the reference took effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A PointAtWhichAPublicationIsRead
`s 69(1) the reference is to the publication as in force or current on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `a particular day is specified for that purpose in the Act or instrument`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN AsInForceOrCurrentOnTheDay specified
    WHEN NOTHING THEN AsInForceOrCurrentOnTheDay `the day on which the provision containing the reference took effect`

-- src:739 | (2) Notwithstanding subsection (1), a reference in any Act or instrument to a publication extends to the publication, as in force for the time being—
-- src:740 | (a) if that intention appears in the Act or instrument, and
-- src:741 | (b) where that intention appears in the instrument—if the Act under which the instrument is made provides that such instruments may apply, adopt or incorporate publications, as in force for the time being.
@ref s 69(2) (src:739-741)
GIVEN `the intention that the reference extends to the publication as in force for the time being appears in the Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intention appears in an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act under which the instrument is made provides that such instruments may apply, adopt or incorporate publications as in force for the time being` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 69(2) the reference extends to the publication, as in force for the time being` MEANS
    IF NOT `the intention that the reference extends to the publication as in force for the time being appears in the Act or instrument`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the intention appears in an instrument`
         THEN JUST `the Act under which the instrument is made provides that such instruments may apply, adopt or incorporate publications as in force for the time being`
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `69A Evidence of publication of Australian standards or other publications`

DECLARE WayOfGivingEvidenceOfAPublication IS ONE OF
    ByAPurportedCopyPublishedByOrOnBehalfOfTheBodyOrPerson
    ByAPurportedCopyPublishedOnTheWebsiteOrInTheGazetteOrPrintedByAuthorityOfAGovernment
    ByAnotherWayOfGivingEvidence

-- src:744 | If an Act or statutory rule applies, adopts or incorporates by way of reference any publication, or any provision of a publication, of Standards Australia, any other body or any person expressly or impliedly identified in the Act or statutory rule, evidence of the publication or provision may be given in any proceedings—
-- src:745 | (a) by the production of a document purporting to be a copy of it and purporting to be published by or on behalf of Standards Australia or the other body or person concerned, or
-- src:746 | (b) by the production of a document purporting to be a copy of it and purporting to be published on the NSW legislation website or in the Gazette, or printed by the authority of the Government of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory.
@ref s 69A (src:744-746)
GIVEN `an Act or statutory rule applies, adopts or incorporates by way of reference a publication, or a provision of a publication, of Standards Australia, any other body or any person expressly or impliedly identified in the Act or statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A WayOfGivingEvidenceOfAPublication
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 69A evidence of the publication or provision may be given in proceedings in that way` MEANS
    IF `an Act or statutory rule applies, adopts or incorporates by way of reference a publication, or a provision of a publication, of Standards Australia, any other body or any person expressly or impliedly identified in the Act or statutory rule`
    THEN CONSIDER way
         WHEN ByAPurportedCopyPublishedByOrOnBehalfOfTheBodyOrPerson THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN ByAPurportedCopyPublishedOnTheWebsiteOrInTheGazetteOrPrintedByAuthorityOfAGovernment THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN ByAnotherWayOfGivingEvidence THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `70 References to changed short titles, names and citations`

-- src:751 | If the short title, name or citation of an Act or instrument is changed, a reference to the short title, name or citation in any other Act or instrument or in a document of any kind shall be read as a reference to the short title, name or citation as changed.
@ref s 70 (src:751)
GIVEN `the short title, name or citation of an Act or instrument is changed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70 a reference to the short title, name or citation is read as a reference to the short title, name or citation as changed` MEANS
    IF `the short title, name or citation of an Act or instrument is changed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `71 Time of expiry of temporary Acts and instruments`

-- Computed in nsw-interpretation-time.l4 as `s 71 the moment an Act or instrument expressed to expire or remain in force until a day stops operating`.

§§ `72 Retrospective commencement of continuing Acts`

-- src:757 | (1) If a Bill for an Act to continue a temporary Act has been introduced into Parliament and is still pending at the expiration of the temporary Act, the Act shall, on the date of its assent, be deemed to have taken effect in continuing the temporary Act on the expiration of the temporary Act.
@ref s 72(1) (src:757)
GIVEN `a Bill for an Act to continue a temporary Act has been introduced into Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Bill is still pending at the expiration of the temporary Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(1) the Act is deemed on the date of its assent to have taken effect in continuing the temporary Act on the expiration of the temporary Act` MEANS
    IF `a Bill for an Act to continue a temporary Act has been introduced into Parliament` AND `the Bill is still pending at the expiration of the temporary Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:758 | (2) This section does not make any person liable to any penalty for or in respect of a contravention of the temporary Act that occurs after the expiration of the temporary Act and before the date of assent to the Act by which the temporary Act is continued.
@ref s 72(2) (src:758)
GIVEN `the day of the contravention of the temporary Act` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the temporary Act` IS A DATE
      `the date of assent to the Act by which the temporary Act is continued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(2) section 72 makes the person liable to a penalty for the contravention of the temporary Act` MEANS
    IF Day `the day of the contravention of the temporary Act` GREATER THAN Day `the last day of the temporary Act` AND Day `the day of the contravention of the temporary Act` LESS THAN Day `the date of assent to the Act by which the temporary Act is continued`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `73 Private Acts not to affect rights of the Crown etc`

-- src:761 | (1) A Private Act that is passed after the commencement of this Act shall not be construed so as—
-- src:762 | (a) to affect, in a manner prejudicial to the Crown or any other person (other than a person at whose instance or for whose special benefit the Act is passed or some other person claiming by, through or under such a person), the rights of the Crown or any such other person existing before the passing of the Act, or
@ref s 73(1)(a) (src:761-762)
GIVEN `the Private Act is passed after the commencement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Crown or another person other than a person at whose instance or for whose special benefit the Act is passed or a person claiming by, through or under such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Private Act would affect in a manner prejudicial to the person the rights of the person existing before the passing of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(1)(a) the Private Act is construed so as to affect the rights of the person` MEANS
    IF `the Private Act is passed after the commencement of this Act` AND `the person is the Crown or another person other than a person at whose instance or for whose special benefit the Act is passed or a person claiming by, through or under such a person` AND `the Private Act would affect in a manner prejudicial to the person the rights of the person existing before the passing of the Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:761 | (1) A Private Act that is passed after the commencement of this Act shall not be construed so as—
-- src:762 | (a) to affect, in a manner prejudicial to the Crown or any other person (other than a person at whose instance or for whose special benefit the Act is passed or some other person claiming by, through or under such a person), the rights of the Crown or any such other person existing before the passing of the Act, or
-- src:763 | (b) to impose liabilities on the Crown or any other person (other than a person at whose instance or for whose special benefit the Act is passed or some other person claiming by, through or under such a person) in respect of any thing done or omitted to be done before the passing of the Act.
@ref s 73(1)(b) (src:761-763)
GIVEN `the Private Act is passed after the commencement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Crown or another person other than a person at whose instance or for whose special benefit the Act is passed or a person claiming by, through or under such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Private Act would impose liabilities on the person in respect of any thing done or omitted to be done before the passing of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(1)(b) the Private Act is construed so as to impose liabilities on the person` MEANS
    IF `the Private Act is passed after the commencement of this Act` AND `the person is the Crown or another person other than a person at whose instance or for whose special benefit the Act is passed or a person claiming by, through or under such a person` AND `the Private Act would impose liabilities on the person in respect of any thing done or omitted to be done before the passing of the Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE ProvisionThatContinuesToApply IS ONE OF
    Section17OfTheActsShorteningActOf1852
    Section14OfTheInterpretationAct1897
    SomeOtherProvisionNotNamedInSection73

-- src:764 | (2) Without limiting the effect of section 30—
-- src:765 | (a) the provisions of section 17 of the Act 16 Victoria No 1 (the Acts Shortening Act of 1852) continue to apply in relation to the rights of the Crown and any other person, being rights that would, but for those provisions, be affected by the passing of Private Acts to which that Act applied before the commencement of this Act, and
-- src:766 | (b) the provisions of section 14 of the Interpretation Act 1897 continue to apply in relation to the rights of the Crown and any other person, being rights that would, but for those provisions, be affected by the passing of Private Acts to which that Act applied before the commencement of this Act,
-- src:767 | notwithstanding the repeal of those Acts by this Act.
@ref s 73(2) (src:764-767)
GIVEN provision IS A ProvisionThatContinuesToApply
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(2) the provision continues to apply in relation to the rights of the Crown and any other person notwithstanding the repeal of the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN Section17OfTheActsShorteningActOf1852 THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN Section14OfTheInterpretationAct1897 THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN SomeOtherProvisionNotNamedInSection73 THEN NOTHING

§§ `74 Private Acts amended by Public Acts do not thereby become Public Acts`

-- src:770 | A Private Act does not become a Public Act merely because it has been amended by or under a Public Act.
@ref s 74 (src:770)
GIVEN `the Private Act has been amended by or under a Public Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74 the Private Act becomes a Public Act merely because of the amendment` MEANS
    IF `the Private Act has been amended by or under a Public Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `75 Publication of statutory notices`

-- src:773 | If an Act or statutory rule requires a notice or advertisement to be published in the Gazette and in one or more newspapers or other location, it is sufficient compliance with the requirement if—
-- src:774 | (a) the notice or advertisement is published in the Gazette, and
-- src:775 | (b) there is published in each newspaper or other location—
-- src:776 | (i) a summary of the notice or advertisement, or
-- src:777 | (ii) a statement to the effect that the notice or advertisement has been published in the Gazette,
-- src:778 | together with a reference to the date of publication of the Gazette in which the notice or advertisement has been published.
@ref s 75 (src:773-778)
GIVEN `an Act or statutory rule requires a notice or advertisement to be published in the Gazette and in one or more newspapers or other location` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice or advertisement is published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is published in each newspaper or other location a summary of the notice or advertisement, or a statement to the effect that it has been published in the Gazette, together with a reference to the date of publication of the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75 the requirement is sufficiently complied with` MEANS
    IF `an Act or statutory rule requires a notice or advertisement to be published in the Gazette and in one or more newspapers or other location`
    THEN IF `the notice or advertisement is published in the Gazette` AND `there is published in each newspaper or other location a summary of the notice or advertisement, or a statement to the effect that it has been published in the Gazette, together with a reference to the date of publication of the Gazette`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `76 Service by post`

-- src:781 | (1) If an Act or instrument authorises or requires any document to be served by post (whether the word "serve", "give" or "send" or any other word is used), service of the document—
-- src:782 | (a) may be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting a letter containing the document, and
@ref s 76(1)(a) (src:781-782)
GIVEN `an Act or instrument authorises or requires a document to be served by post` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter containing the document is properly addressed, prepaid and posted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(1)(a) service of the document may be effected by posting the letter` MEANS
    IF `an Act or instrument authorises or requires a document to be served by post`
    THEN IF `the letter containing the document is properly addressed, prepaid and posted` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:781 | (1) If an Act or instrument authorises or requires any document to be served by post (whether the word "serve", "give" or "send" or any other word is used), service of the document—
-- src:782 | (a) may be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting a letter containing the document, and
-- src:783 | (b) in Australia or in an external Territory—is, unless evidence sufficient to raise doubt is adduced to the contrary, taken to have been effected on the seventh working day after the letter was posted, and
@ref s 76(1)(b) (src:781-783)
GIVEN `an Act or instrument authorises or requires a document to be served by post` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter containing the document was properly addressed, prepaid and posted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter was posted in Australia or in an external Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `evidence sufficient to raise doubt is adduced to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the letter was posted` IS A DATE
      `public and bank holidays in the place to which the letter was addressed` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 76(1)(b) the day service is taken to have been effected` MEANS
    IF `an Act or instrument authorises or requires a document to be served by post` AND `the letter containing the document was properly addressed, prepaid and posted` AND `the letter was posted in Australia or in an external Territory` AND (NOT `evidence sufficient to raise doubt is adduced to the contrary`)
    THEN JUST (`s 76(1)(b) the day service by post in Australia or an external Territory is taken to be effected` `the day the letter was posted` `public and bank holidays in the place to which the letter was addressed`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:781 | (1) If an Act or instrument authorises or requires any document to be served by post (whether the word "serve", "give" or "send" or any other word is used), service of the document—
-- src:782 | (a) may be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting a letter containing the document, and
-- src:783 | (b) in Australia or in an external Territory—is, unless evidence sufficient to raise doubt is adduced to the contrary, taken to have been effected on the seventh working day after the letter was posted, and
-- src:784 | (c) in another place—is, unless evidence sufficient to raise doubt is adduced to the contrary, taken to have been effected at the time when the letter would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post.
@ref s 76(1)(c) (src:781-784)
GIVEN `an Act or instrument authorises or requires a document to be served by post` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter containing the document was properly addressed, prepaid and posted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter was posted in another place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `evidence sufficient to raise doubt is adduced to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the letter would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 76(1)(c) the day service in another place is taken to have been effected` MEANS
    IF `an Act or instrument authorises or requires a document to be served by post` AND `the letter containing the document was properly addressed, prepaid and posted` AND `the letter was posted in another place` AND (NOT `evidence sufficient to raise doubt is adduced to the contrary`)
    THEN JUST `the day on which the letter would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `77 Registered post etc not necessary in the case of Acts and statutory rules passed etc before 24.4.1969`

-- src:791 | (1) Any Act or statutory rule under which a document (other than a summons) may be or is required to be served on a person by registered mail, registered post, certified mail or certified post (whether the word "serve", "give" or "send" or any other word is used) shall be taken to authorise the service of the document by post (other than registered mail, registered post, certified mail or certified post) in addition to any other means by which the Act or statutory rule authorises the document to be served.
-- src:792 | (2) Subsection (1)—
-- src:793 | (a) applies only to Acts and statutory rules enacted or made before 24 April 1969 (being the day on which the Interpretation (Amendment) Act 1969 commenced), and
-- src:794 | (b) so applies notwithstanding any provision of any such Act or statutory rule.
-- src:795 | (3) The Governor may, by order published in the Gazette, declare that subsection (1) does not apply to any specified Act or statutory rule or to any specified provision of any specified Act or statutory rule.
-- src:796 | (4) An order in force under subsection (3) does not affect the operation of subsection (1) in relation to the service of a document that was posted before the order was made.
@ref s 77 (src:791-796)
GIVEN `the document is a summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act or statutory rule allows or requires the document to be served by registered mail, registered post, certified mail or certified post` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Act or statutory rule was enacted or made` IS A DATE
      `an order under section 77(3) declares that section 77(1) does not apply to the Act or statutory rule or to the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document was posted before that order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(1) the Act or statutory rule is taken to authorise the service of the document by post other than registered mail, registered post, certified mail or certified post` MEANS
    IF NOT (Day `the day the Act or statutory rule was enacted or made` LESS THAN Day (Date 24 4 1969))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the document is a summons`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF `an order under section 77(3) declares that section 77(1) does not apply to the Act or statutory rule or to the provision` AND (NOT `the document was posted before that order was made`)
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF `the Act or statutory rule allows or requires the document to be served by registered mail, registered post, certified mail or certified post` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:795 | (3) The Governor may, by order published in the Gazette, declare that subsection (1) does not apply to any specified Act or statutory rule or to any specified provision of any specified Act or statutory rule.
@ref s 77(3) (src:795)
GIVEN `the declaration is made by order published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(3) the Governor may declare that section 77(1) does not apply to a specified Act or statutory rule or to a specified provision` MEANS
    IF `the declaration is made by order published in the Gazette` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `78 Rules of court`

-- src:799 | (1) The power of a person or body to make rules of court includes power to make rules of court for the purposes of any Act or statutory rule that permits or requires any thing to be done by or in accordance with rules of court.
@ref s 78(1) (src:799)
GIVEN `an Act or statutory rule permits or requires a thing to be done by or in accordance with rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(1) the power of a person or body to make rules of court includes power to make rules of court for the purposes of the Act or statutory rule` MEANS
    IF `an Act or statutory rule permits or requires a thing to be done by or in accordance with rules of court` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:800 | (2) If an Act or statutory rule—
-- src:801 | (a) confers any jurisdiction on a court or tribunal, or
-- src:802 | (b) extends or varies the jurisdiction of a court or tribunal,
-- src:803 | the person or body having power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of the court or tribunal may make rules or orders (including rules or orders with respect to costs) regulating the practice and procedure of the court or tribunal in the exercise of the jurisdiction so conferred, extended or varied.
@ref s 78(2) (src:800-803)
GIVEN `an Act or statutory rule confers jurisdiction on a court or tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an Act or statutory rule extends or varies the jurisdiction of a court or tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(2) the person or body having power to make rules or orders regulating practice and procedure may make rules or orders, including with respect to costs, for the jurisdiction so conferred, extended or varied` MEANS
    IF `an Act or statutory rule confers jurisdiction on a court or tribunal` OR `an Act or statutory rule extends or varies the jurisdiction of a court or tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `79 Authority to administer oaths`

DECLARE AuthorityOfAHearingBody IS ONE OF
    AuthorityToReceiveEvidence
    AuthorityToQuestionWitnessesAndToAdministerOathsToWitnessesLawfullyCalled
    SomeOtherAuthorityOfAHearingBody

-- src:806 | Any person or body authorised by law, or by consent of parties, to conduct a hearing for the purpose of the determination (by that or any other person or body) of any matter or thing shall have authority—
-- src:807 | (a) to receive evidence, and
-- src:808 | (b) to examine witnesses, and to administer oaths to witnesses, who have been lawfully called before that person or body.
@ref s 79 (src:806-808)
GIVEN `the person or body is authorised by law, or by consent of parties, to conduct a hearing for the purpose of the determination of a matter or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      authority IS A AuthorityOfAHearingBody
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79 the person or body has the authority` MEANS
    IF `the person or body is authorised by law, or by consent of parties, to conduct a hearing for the purpose of the determination of a matter or thing`
    THEN CONSIDER authority
         WHEN AuthorityToReceiveEvidence THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN AuthorityToQuestionWitnessesAndToAdministerOathsToWitnessesLawfullyCalled THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN SomeOtherAuthorityOfAHearingBody THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `80 Compliance with forms`

-- src:811 | (1) If a form is prescribed by, or approved under, an Act or statutory rule, strict compliance with the form is not necessary but substantial compliance is sufficient.
@ref s 80(1) strict compliance (src:811)
GIVEN `a form is prescribed by, or approved under, an Act or statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(1) strict compliance with the form is necessary` MEANS
    IF `a form is prescribed by, or approved under, an Act or statutory rule` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:811 | (1) If a form is prescribed by, or approved under, an Act or statutory rule, strict compliance with the form is not necessary but substantial compliance is sufficient.
@ref s 80(1) substantial compliance (src:811)
GIVEN `a form is prescribed by, or approved under, an Act or statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(1) substantial compliance with the form is sufficient` MEANS
    IF `a form is prescribed by, or approved under, an Act or statutory rule` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:812 | (2) If a form prescribed by, or approved under, an Act or instrument requires the form to be completed in a specified manner, or requires specified information to be included in, attached to or furnished with the form, the form is not duly completed unless it is completed in that manner and unless it includes, or has attached to or furnished with it, that information.
@ref s 80(2) (src:812)
GIVEN `the form requires it to be completed in a specified manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is completed in that manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form requires specified information to be included in, attached to or furnished with the form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it includes, or has attached to or furnished with it, that information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(2) the form is duly completed` MEANS
    IF (`the form requires it to be completed in a specified manner` AND (NOT `it is completed in that manner`)) OR (`the form requires specified information to be included in, attached to or furnished with the form` AND (NOT `it includes, or has attached to or furnished with it, that information`))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:813 | (3) Without limiting the generality of subsections (1) and (2), in any form in, or approved under, an Act or statutory rule, a reference to a date that is presumed to be in the nineteenth or twentieth century may be construed as a reference to a date in the twenty-first century and the form may be altered accordingly.
@ref s 80(3) (src:813)
GIVEN `it is a reference, in a form in or approved under an Act or statutory rule, to a date that is presumed to be in the nineteenth or twentieth century` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(3) the reference may be construed as a reference to a date in the twenty-first century and the form may be altered accordingly` MEANS
    IF `it is a reference, in a form in or approved under an Act or statutory rule, to a date that is presumed to be in the nineteenth or twentieth century` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:814 | (4) If an Act or statutory rule requires anything to be in a form prescribed by rules of court (whether generally or in relation to a particular court or tribunal), any such rules of court may instead provide for the thing to be in a form approved under or in accordance with those rules.
@ref s 80(4) (src:814)
GIVEN `an Act or statutory rule requires a thing to be in a form prescribed by rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(4) the rules of court may instead provide for the thing to be in a form approved under or in accordance with those rules` MEANS
    IF `an Act or statutory rule requires a thing to be in a form prescribed by rules of court` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `80A Maximum monetary penalty Local Court may impose in certain circumstances`

-- src:817 | If an Act—
-- src:818 | (a) provides that an offence under the Act may be dealt with summarily by the Local Court or, in the alternative, by another court, and
-- src:819 | (b) imposes a limit by reference solely to an amount of money (however expressed) on the penalty that the Local Court may impose when dealing with such an offence,
-- src:820 | that limit, unless otherwise expressly provided by the Act, does not affect any non-monetary penalty that may be imposed by the Local Court for the offence.
@ref s 80A (src:817-820)
GIVEN `an Act provides that an offence under the Act may be dealt with summarily by the Local Court or, in the alternative, by another court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act imposes a limit by reference solely to an amount of money, however expressed, on the penalty that the Local Court may impose when dealing with such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act otherwise expressly provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80A the limit affects a non-monetary penalty that may be imposed by the Local Court for the offence` MEANS
    IF `an Act provides that an offence under the Act may be dealt with summarily by the Local Court or, in the alternative, by another court` AND `the Act imposes a limit by reference solely to an amount of money, however expressed, on the penalty that the Local Court may impose when dealing with such an offence` AND (NOT `the Act otherwise expressly provides`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `82 Repeals`

-- src:825 | Each Act specified in Schedule 2 is, to the extent indicated in that Schedule, repealed.
@ref s 82 (src:825)
GIVEN `the Act is specified in Schedule 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82 the Act is repealed to the extent indicated in Schedule 2` MEANS
    IF `the Act is specified in Schedule 2` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `83 Savings and transitional provisions`

-- src:828 | Schedule 3 has effect.
@ref s 83 (src:828)
GIVEN `it is a provision of Schedule 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83 the provision has effect` MEANS
    IF `it is a provision of Schedule 3` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

